      "message": "p2p: enforce relay limit for BIP35 requesters\n\nWhen a node offers `NODE_BLOOM`, an inbound peer advertising `fRelay=false` can request mempool inventory while remaining outside inbound transaction-relay capacity.\n\nEnforce the limit when an inbound peer first requests BIP35 mempool inventory, avoiding repeated scans of all connections on subsequent requests.\nKeep `fRelay=false` effective for ongoing transaction announcements.\nSkip the response when capacity eviction selects the requester.",
